  [tgt
    'the way back through fromAST writes the space a name needs from the prose after it, so a known command never turns unknown on the way back, by the inclusion the Regent decided on 2026-10-25; an ORD of the batch the version moves once for'
  [/tgt]
  [ctx
    'measured at d739544, section 3 of the intake: fromAST writes a text child glued to the name of the command that holds it, so a context command holding the prose foo comes back as the unknown command ctxfoo; and a mood header before prose reads the first word of the prose as one more mood code'
  [/ctx]
  [cnst
    'two pieces written side by side read as one when a name ends the first and a name starts the second, or the first ends a mood header; a space between them is what the source had, and whitespace between tokens is no node, so it costs nothing on the way in'
  [/cnst]
  [cnst
